.TH GEN 1 "2025-01-27" "content-generator v0.1.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
gen \- Content Generator for Educational Course Materials

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gen
.I command
[options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gen
is a command-line tool for generating educational course content, including learning materials, assessment tools, and academic documentation. It supports multiple course types including TAFE, commercial training, and accelerated learning programs.

The tool can initialize new courses, generate academic documents, manage configuration files, convert between markdown and notebooks, and list available AI models for content generation.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS init
Initialize a new course content folder with specified parameters.

.B gen init
.BI --course-name " NAME"
[options]

.TP
.BR \-n ", " --course-name " NAME"
Course name (required)

.TP
.BR \-t ", " --target " PATH"
Target directory for course content (default: current directory)

.TP
.BR \-u ", " --uoc-codes " CODE1,CODE2,..."
Units of Competency codes to include

.TP
.BR \-m ", " --mission " PROMPT"
Mission prompt for course content generation

.TP
.BR \-\-no-llm
Disable language model generation (use templates only)

.TP
.BR \-i ", " --model " MODEL"
AI model for content generation (default: gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14)
.br
Examples: gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14, gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4o, claude-3-5-sonnet

.TP
.BR \-\-course-type " TYPE"
Course type: TAFE, COMMERCIAL, ACCELERATED, CUSTOM (default: TAFE)

.TP
.BR \-\-num-weeks " WEEKS"
Total number of weeks (default: 20)

.TP
.BR \-\-academic-weeks " WEEKS"
Academic weeks (default: 18)

.TP
.BR \-\-reassessment-weeks " WEEKS"
Reassessment weeks (default: 2)

.TP
.BR \-\-delivery-location " LOCATION"
Primary delivery location (campus, city, etc.)

.TP
.BR \-\-delivery-mode " MODE"
Delivery mode: face-to-face, online, hybrid (default: face-to-face)

.TP
.BR \-\-institution-name " NAME"
Institution name for course materials

.TP
.BR \-\-student-cohort " DESCRIPTION"
Target student cohort description

.TP
.BR \-\-config-file " PATH"
Path to JSON/YAML configuration file

.TP
.BR \-\-theme " PATH"
CSS theme file for presentations (default: northmetro.css)

.SS push
Push key academic documents to the generated content folder for archive in content collection.

.B gen push
[.BI --target " PATH"]

.TP
.BR \-t ", " --target " PATH"
Path to the course content folder to process (default: current directory)

.SS config
Create and manage course configuration files.

.B gen config
[options]

.TP
.BR \-c ", " --create " NAME"
Create a new configuration file with the specified name (default: course_config.yaml)

.TP
.BR \-t ", " --template " TYPE"
Template type: basic, tafe, commercial, accelerated, custom (default: basic)

.TP
.BR \-o ", " --output-dir " PATH"
Output directory for the configuration file (default: current directory)

.SS convert
Convert markdown files to Jupyter notebooks or vice versa using jupytext.

.B gen convert
.I course_directory
[options]

.TP
.BI course_directory
Path to the course content folder

.TP
.BR \-\-pattern " PATTERN"
File pattern to convert (default: demo.md)

.TP
.BR \-\-reverse
Convert notebooks to markdown instead

.SS list-models
List all available AI models for content generation.

.B gen list-models

Displays all available models from OpenAI, Anthropic, and HuggingFace providers, with caching for 24 hours to avoid repeated API calls.

.SH AI MODEL SELECTION

The tool supports multiple AI providers and models for content generation:

.SS Default Model
.B gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14
- Cheapest option, good for basic content generation

.SS Popular Models
.TP
.B OpenAI
- gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4o, gpt-4-turbo
.TP
.B Anthropic
- claude-3-5-sonnet, claude-3-opus, claude-3-haiku
.TP
.B HuggingFace
- meta-llama/Llama-3.2-*, deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3

.SS Model Selection Examples
.EX
# Use cheapest model (default)
gen init --course-name "Course"

# Use specific OpenAI model
gen init --course-name "Course" --model "gpt-4o"

# Use Claude model
gen init --course-name "Course" --model "claude-3-5-sonnet"

# List all available models
gen list-models
.EE

.SH TEMPLATE TYPES

.SS basic
Simple template with placeholders for customization. Includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
20-week course structure
.IP \[bu]
Basic assessment framework
.IP \[bu]
Placeholder sections for units and learning phases

.SS tafe
Pre-configured for TAFE delivery with units of competency. Includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
TAFE-specific course structure (20 weeks)
.IP \[bu]
Common AI/ML UOC codes (ICTAII401, ICTAII501, ICTAII502)
.IP \[bu]
TAFE assessment best practices
.IP \[bu]
Structured learning phases for vocational training

.SS commercial
Optimized for professional training and upskilling. Includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
12-week intensive structure
.IP \[bu]
Hybrid delivery focus
.IP \[bu]
Professional assessment framework
.IP \[bu]
Skill-based learning phases

.SS accelerated
Fast-paced intensive learning program. Includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
8-week compressed structure
.IP \[bu]
Online delivery focus
.IP \[bu]
Rapid assessment framework
.IP \[bu]
Intensive learning phases

.SS custom
Fully customizable template for unique requirements. Includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
Flexible 16-week structure
.IP \[bu]
Customizable assessment types
.IP \[bu]
User-defined learning phases
.IP \[bu]
Additional custom configuration options

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

The tool uses several environment variables for configuration:

.TP
.B COURSE_CONTENT
Path to course content directory (required for production)

.TP
.B OUTPUT_LOCATION
Path to output directory (required for production)

.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
OpenAI API key for AI content generation (optional)

.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Anthropic API key for AI content generation (optional)

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Initialize a basic TAFE course
.EX
gen init --course-name "AI Fundamentals" --uoc-codes ICTAII401,ICTAII501
.EE

.SS Initialize with specific AI model
.EX
gen init --course-name "AI Course" --model "gpt-4o" --uoc-codes ICTAII401,ICTAII501
.EE

.SS Initialize with configuration file
.EX
gen init --course-name "Machine Learning" --config-file my_config.yaml
.EE

.SS Initialize template-only course (no AI generation)
.EX
gen init --course-name "Template Course" --no-llm
.EE

.SS Create a TAFE configuration template
.EX
gen config --template tafe --create tafe_course_config
.EE

.SS Create a basic configuration with defaults
.EX
gen config
.EE

.SS Initialize commercial course with custom parameters
.EX
gen init --course-name "Data Science Bootcamp" \\
    --course-type COMMERCIAL \\
    --num-weeks 12 \\
    --delivery-mode hybrid \\
    --institution-name "Tech Academy" \\
    --student-cohort "Professional developers seeking upskilling"
.EE

.SS Generate documents for existing course
.EX
gen push --target /path/to/course/folder
.EE

.SS Convert markdown files to notebooks
.EX
gen convert /path/to/course --pattern "*.md"
.EE

.SS Convert notebooks back to markdown
.EX
gen convert /path/to/course --reverse
.EE

.SS List available AI models
.EX
gen list-models
.EE

.SH FILES

.TP
.B course_config.yaml
Course configuration file (created by gen config)

.TP
.B northmetro.css
Default CSS theme for presentations

.TP
.B templates/
Directory containing document templates

